### Description

The type initializer sometimes doesn't execute for an empty struct, and the behavior is not consistent across different platforms + configurations. 

### Reproduction Steps

Repro:

```cs
var foo = new Foo<Bar>();
Console.WriteLine(foo.ToString());
Console.WriteLine(Bar.X);

struct Foo<T> where T : IBar
{
    static Foo()
    {
        T.Set();
    }
}

struct Bar : IBar
{
    public static int X;
    public static void Set()
    {
        X = 42;
    }
}

interface IBar
{
    abstract static void Set();
}
```

Note that the line `foo.ToString()` does an invocation to the virtual method. So according to ECMA:

```
If not marked BeforeFieldInit then that type’s initializer method is executed at
...
- first invocation of any instance or virtual method of that type if it is a value type
```

BTW the abstract static method and generic here is not necessary for the repro, the below code also reproduces this issue:

```cs
var foo = new Foo();
Console.WriteLine(foo.ToString());
Console.WriteLine(Bar.X);

struct Foo
{
    static Foo()
    {
        Bar.Set();
    }
}

struct Bar
{
    public static int X;
    public static void Set()
    {
        X = 42;
    }
}
```

### Expected behavior

Always prints
```
Foo`1[Bar]
42
```

### Actual behavior

The output from `Bar.X`:

| Platform | Configuration | TieredCompilation | Output |
| -- | -- | -- | -- |
| win-x64 | Debug | N/A | `0` |
| win-x64 | Release | true | `0` |
| win-x64 | Release | false | `0` |
| linux-x64 | Debug | N/A | `42` |
| linux-x64 | Release | true | `42` |
| linux-x64 | Release | false | `0` |
| linux-arm64 | Debug | N/A | `42` |
| linux-arm64 | Release | true | `42` |
| linux-arm64 | Release | false | `0` |
| osx-arm64 | Debug | N/A | `42` |
| osx-arm64 | Release | true | `42` |
| osx-arm64 | Release | false | `0` |

